<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayabaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1135–<a href="/years/1157">1157</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Joyoboyo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayabaya was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kediri-kingdom">Kediri</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a> in the mid 12th century. An inscription of 1135 records his victory over Janggala with the words Panjalu jayati, Panjalu is victorious, uniting the realm <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/airlangga">Airlangga</a> had divided. His court produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-javanese">Old Javanese</a> poem Bharatayuddha, and later Javanese tradition attributed to him a famous book of prophecies.</p></div>
